{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I will greatly multiply your sorrow.</b> The blood of menstruation, called נִדַּת דְּוֹתָהּ (Leviticus 12:2), for indeed she is then כָּל הַיּוֹם דָּוָה (Lamentations 1:13)." "<b>And your pregnancy.</b> The reverse of what it was before the sin, as they said: on the day they were created, on that day they had relations, on that day they brought forth offspring (Genesis Rabbah 22:2). And the like of this they said will be in the future, as they said: in the future a woman will give birth every day (Shabbat 30b) — for indeed Israel will be accepted before the blessed El as Adam the first man was before his sin." "<b>In sorrow you shall bring forth children.</b> You shall raise them in greater distress than other living creatures. For indeed the term \"bearing\" is used of raising, as it says: חֲמֵשֶׁת בְּנֵי מִיכַל בַּת שָׁאוּל אֲשֶׁר יָלְדָה לְעַדְרִיאֵל (2 Samuel 21:8)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:55.072039225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}